WEBVTT

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:26.270
December. The winter solstice has passed,
and our school was in winter vacation.

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:31.860
With the pairing of the leg shield,
which was originally installed,

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:35.410
and the new windshield that I had put on,

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:39.830
the problem of cold on my Cub
had been largely solved.

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:43.790
Reiko had resisted at first,
saying that they didn't look cool,

00:00:43.790 --> 00:00:47.790
but eventually gave in to the cold
and installed leg shields.

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:55.720
The matter of the cold had been settled,
and we could now ride our Cubs freely.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:59.470
Any time we wanted, wherever
we wanted, just as we had before.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.150
Koguma-<i>san</i>!

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:17.280
Going shopping?

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.080
Yes, up to Nirasaki to buy
some coffee beans.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.540
Be careful.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:24.040
Right!

00:01:30.210 --> 00:01:32.670
She had been moving
forward with her project

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:36.720
to turn her shop's eat-in space
into an Italian bar.

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:39.800
Apparently, she was working
at the post office,

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.970
and had been scouring the town
for things she could use in her bar.

00:02:21.350 --> 00:02:23.140
Brr...

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:34.650
That day, spread out before my gaze...

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:37.950
...for the first time since
I started riding my Cub...

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:41.110
...was a whole world of silver.

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:31.060
I can't ride in this.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.760
"Reiko"

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.060
--Hello--
--Come on over, now!

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.020
--No way.
--Just come over!

00:05:16.020 --> 00:05:18.860
I've got something here
that's a ton of fun!

00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.740
"Look at this!!"
"Open attached image"

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:30.740
"Open attached image"

00:05:39.880 --> 00:05:40.630
Hello.

00:05:40.630 --> 00:05:42.590
I'll be right over.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:29.860
Welcome.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:34.160
Is that it?

00:07:34.160 --> 00:07:38.000
Yep. Tire chains for a Super Cub.

00:07:40.620 --> 00:07:44.210
Where did you come by
something like those?

00:07:44.210 --> 00:07:48.300
I heard that the newspaper distributor
in Sagamihara was going out of business,

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:51.840
so I went to see if maybe I could
score some parts for our Cubs,

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:53.760
but I was a little too late.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:56.050
The chassis and parts
had all been taken away,

00:07:56.050 --> 00:07:59.560
and all that was left was this
dead weight that nobody bid on.

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:01.060
Hmm...

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:07.230
At least I thought it was, but I wasn't
expecting it to come in handy so soon.

00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:11.320
You want to put yours on, too?

00:08:11.320 --> 00:08:12.990
Yes!

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:17.740
"Check the configuration
of your tire chains!"

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:20.750
"Before putting them on,
understand their design."

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:48.940
Mm-hmm.

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:08.420
Where are we going?

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:12.260
If we head on up higher,
there's the coolest place.

00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.930
Up?

00:10:22.330 --> 00:10:24.080
Here we go!

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:32.380
Yahoo!

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.590
"Super Cub"
"Episode 10"

00:10:34.590 --> 00:10:38.010
"Snow"

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:16.920
Woo-hoo!

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:44.970
In exchange for the chains,
right? All of it?

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:47.510
Just half, dummy.

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:56.400
It's still a little bit warm.

00:13:05.780 --> 00:13:07.320
Here.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:09.030
Thanks.

00:13:30.810 --> 00:13:32.720
Here goes!

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:34.430
Whoo!

00:14:00.540 --> 00:14:02.000
Not good enough!

00:14:03.510 --> 00:14:05.590
Come on, come on!

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:08.930
Why, you...!

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:18.270
Whoa! Using your Cub is foul play!

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:20.520
You're the one who started it!

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:24.230
All right, all right, I give up!

00:14:24.230 --> 00:14:27.280
Easy! I said I give up!

00:14:36.290 --> 00:14:38.330
This feels so good!

00:14:40.130 --> 00:14:42.000
Hey, having fun?

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:44.380
Mm-hmm, I am.

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:52.800
Winter is fun, huh?

00:14:52.800 --> 00:14:54.520
Mm-hmm.

00:14:54.520 --> 00:14:58.060
When you have a Cub, winter is fun.

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:10.860
Ready to go?

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:13.700
Mm-hmm.

00:15:27.380 --> 00:15:30.550
Ah, Reiko-<i>chan</i>, Koguma-<i>san</i>!

00:15:31.640 --> 00:15:35.180
Ahem... This way, please.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:37.020
All right.

00:15:42.100 --> 00:15:43.650
Huh?

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:46.650
Hmm? What's the matter?

00:15:46.650 --> 00:15:49.950
Something seems different from usual.

00:15:51.740 --> 00:15:54.320
It's the tablecloth and chairs.

00:15:54.320 --> 00:15:56.490
The Tricolore flag colors.

00:15:56.490 --> 00:16:01.330
It looks like Italy is steadily
enlarging its territory.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:03.290
Yes.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:06.750
Aw, I wish you would have
invited me to come, too.

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:09.050
You couldn't have made it on a bicycle.

00:16:09.050 --> 00:16:11.760
I probably would have been
fine on my Moulton.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:14.090
Maybe I'll go up there sometime.

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:17.220
I'll come with you when you do.

00:16:17.220 --> 00:16:21.770
Next time, I'll let you ride with me,
and we'll go up and down Mt. Kaikoma.

00:16:21.770 --> 00:16:24.350
I have the perfect "seat" for you, too.

00:16:24.350 --> 00:16:26.520
"Seat"?

00:16:28.320 --> 00:16:30.150
In <i>there</i>.

00:16:32.650 --> 00:16:35.120
Whoa, Shii-<i>chan</i>, I'm joking.

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:38.830
Reiko-<i>chan</i>, I don't trust that smile.

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:43.080
She might fit in the front
basket of my Cub, too.

00:16:43.080 --> 00:16:47.040
Huh?! Not you, too, Koguma-<i>san</i>!

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:44.080
Hey, welcome!

00:18:45.160 --> 00:18:46.910
Koguma-<i>san</i>...

00:18:48.000 --> 00:18:51.420
Will Guatemalan French
Roast be okay today?

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:53.460
I'll leave it to you.

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:01.260
Hello.

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:09.020
Thanks for waiting!

00:19:09.020 --> 00:19:10.730
Between the snow and icing,

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:13.400
they say the forest roads
are impassible to vehicles.

00:19:13.400 --> 00:19:17.240
The only ones using them right now
are the deer and wild boar.

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:20.610
The deer and wild boar may not
even be using them anymore.

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:24.490
We don't get too much accumulation
around here, but with the wind...

00:19:24.490 --> 00:19:29.620
Yeah. But for what these cost,
they're worth it.

00:19:30.500 --> 00:19:32.710
Same for these work boots.

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:33.880
Mm-hmm.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:36.510
We have our windshields
and leg shields now,

00:19:36.510 --> 00:19:40.260
and we can ride for hours
without getting cold.

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:43.430
The upgraded shield for
my helmet is also nice.

00:19:43.430 --> 00:19:47.020
Even when the temperature drops,
if we add on the right gear,

00:19:47.020 --> 00:19:49.430
it's nothing we can't deal with.

00:19:51.310 --> 00:19:53.940
Thank you for waiting.

00:19:53.940 --> 00:19:56.360
Here you go.

00:19:56.360 --> 00:19:58.240
Thank you very much.

00:19:58.240 --> 00:20:00.070
Thanks for the coffee.

00:20:02.660 --> 00:20:04.120
Where's Shii-<i>chan </i>today?

00:20:04.120 --> 00:20:08.000
Sorry about that, and after you
came all the way over, too.

00:20:08.000 --> 00:20:09.580
She went out for a bit.

00:20:09.580 --> 00:20:12.580
Ah, the Italian project.

00:20:12.580 --> 00:20:15.500
She likely went into town
to look at a bunch of stuff.

00:20:15.500 --> 00:20:18.050
I saw her turning onto the cat trail.

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:19.510
Cat trail?

00:20:19.510 --> 00:20:22.800
The one that cuts from the prefectural
road through to the Shichiriiwa Line.

00:20:22.800 --> 00:20:25.300
Oh, that narrow little road.

00:20:25.300 --> 00:20:29.350
It's quicker to get to the train
station that way on a bicycle.

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:33.770
I wonder how far Italy
is going to spread now.

00:20:33.770 --> 00:20:38.110
Koguma-<i>san </i>and Reiko-<i>san</i>, it looks like
you two have been an influence on her.

00:20:38.110 --> 00:20:39.940
Hmm?

00:20:39.940 --> 00:20:42.360
She wants to be like the two of you.

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:43.860
Like us?

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:47.830
Yes. She seems to be riding
her bicycle around a lot more,

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:50.540
even when she's not shopping.

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:56.920
Almost as if she's trying
to catch up to you two.

00:20:56.920 --> 00:21:01.260
I'm the one who pushed the
Alex Moulton she's riding on her,

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:03.880
and now that she finally seems
to have taken a liking to it,

00:21:03.880 --> 00:21:06.760
I kind of feel happy about it.

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:15.230
I'm going to stop by Komeri.
How about you?

00:21:15.230 --> 00:21:16.560
Not today.

00:21:16.560 --> 00:21:18.070
Okay.

00:21:21.070 --> 00:21:24.320
It looks like another cold one tomorrow.

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:26.870
Just because we're adding
gear to keep out the cold,

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:31.410
it doesn't mean things
are getting any warmer.

00:21:31.410 --> 00:21:34.160
We had come to realize something...

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:42.260
The real reason why bikers call
winter both a foe and a trial.

00:21:42.260 --> 00:21:48.970
And that... was not because of the cold,
but because of how long it lasts.

00:21:50.310 --> 00:21:55.520
In another few months, spring would
once again come to the Southern Alps,

00:21:55.520 --> 00:21:58.440
and the cherry blossoms would bloom.

00:21:58.440 --> 00:22:06.110
However, for those of us on our Cubs,
spring is still out of reach,

00:22:06.110 --> 00:22:09.450
and too far away to see,
even by squinting.

00:22:20.590 --> 00:22:23.840
"Eniwa Shii"

00:22:25.420 --> 00:22:27.130
Hello?

00:22:32.600 --> 00:22:34.980
...lp... me...

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:36.600
Huh?

00:22:39.770 --> 00:22:41.820
Help me...

00:22:47.910 --> 00:22:50.990
Help... me...

00:24:20.960 --> 00:24:22.880
"A Distant Spring"
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 11"

00:24:22.880 --> 00:24:25.920
"A Distant Spring"
"<i>Super Cub </i>Episode 11"
Episode 11: "A Distant Spring."
